<title>BELGIUM: Unions say Renault case shows laws must be changed.</title>
<headline>Unions say Renault case shows laws must be changed.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Trade Union Confederation said on Tuesday Renault's decision to close its Belgian plant showed European Union employment law governing multinational companies should be changed.</p>
<p>&quot;That means bringing forward the revision of the European Works Council directive from 1999 to now,&quot; the ETUC said in a statement.</p>
<p>ETUC officials were in Luxembourg on Tuesday to meet Prime Minister Jean-Claude Juncker at the start of the Grand Duchy's six-month EU presidency.</p>
